MID_SE_Ism_Die_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_001: You... I knew you were watching. I could sense\nyou lurking.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_002: <NCA>"So, who were those people?"
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_003: Heh. A little late to question my loyalty now.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_004: But sure, I'll answer. They're some people from the\nHar Hali, trying to survive out here.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_005: They broke from their leader, Nuzzuo, and went\ninto hiding.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_006: They're barely making it—and turned to me, of all\npeople, who abandoned them years ago.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_007: The Har Hali have always survived just fine on\ntheir own—living off the forest's blessings.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_008: As this war drags on, nature is weakening. There's\nno other forest they could find.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_009: They told me they were starving. I shared some\nfood with them. That's all.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_010: And in case you are wondering... I don't have faith\nin Balor anymore. Neither do they.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_011: He's a disaster—binding souls, exploiting the living.\nSome idiots will still offer themselves to him...
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_012: But those guys have had enough.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_013: So, believe me now? That I'm not in a shadowy\nalliance with Balor's minions?
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_014: <NCA>"I never doubted you for a second."
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_015: You're too trusting. Heh. No, the problem is...you're\ntoo strong.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_016: You can afford to trust people. You have the\npower to handle even the worst betrayals.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_017: You've got so much power, you can even try to\nsave those who betray you.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_018: Mm...
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_019: I get so sick of that look on your face, so confident\nand knowing... Ugh. If only I had your strength.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_020: Then everything would have been different... What\nhappened with my people... With Orchel...
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_021: <NCA>"You helped those people today."
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_022: With a handful of food? That's not help. It's barely\na handout.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_023: I didn't even want anyone seeing me do it.\nI'm supposed to be the guy who walked away.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_024: What am I doing anyway, helping out those\npeople?
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_025: I told myself they were dead to me. They WERE\ndead to me! But with Bahr Vahn defeated...
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_026: I couldn't help feeling something for those\nstarving fools.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_027: Damn it. Listen to me, weak as they come.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_028: <NCA>"Your heart is strong—full of compassion."
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_029: Compassion? Hmph.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_030: But, maybe... Like Orchel, years ago...
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_031: I've got something to do. I'll catch up with you later.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_032: <NCA>"Give my regards to your people."
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_033: <NCB>"Want some supplies for them?"
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_034: <ACA>Hm. Sure, I'll pass on the message.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_A_035: <ACB>Hm. Yeah, OK. Get the stuff ready.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_S: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Die_S_001: Promised One! You're...you're here!
MID_SE_Ism_Die_S_002: There wasn't a trace of you anywhere. Who knew\nyou'd just appear right out of thin air?
MID_SE_Ism_Die_S_003: <NCA>"Were you waiting here for me?"
MID_SE_Ism_Die_S_004: Urgh... But, OK, yes... Yes, I was.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_S_005: I figured that if you showed up at all, it'd be near\nthe temple here, half dead. I did that once.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_S_006: So, I thought I'd hang around, offer a helping hand.\nBut looks like I was worried for nothing.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_S_007: <NCA>"Well, thank you."
MID_SE_Ism_Die_S_008: <NCB>"That means the world to me."
MID_SE_Ism_Die_S_009: <ACA>No need for that. You're safe. That's all that\nmatters.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_S_010: <ACB>Heh. Really? I should stand around doing nothing\nmore often.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_S_011: Alright. Let's get out of here. Remember those\npeople from the Har Hali I helped?
MID_SE_Ism_Die_S_012: They're kind of following me around now.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_S_013: That'll teach me to throw 'em some scraps and\nsupplies. I mean, I have better things to do!
MID_SE_Ism_Die_S_014: Orchel's getting a real kick out of it, making me\ntake care of those guys.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_S_015: Credna's not helping at all. He just laughs at\nthe trouble they're causing me.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_S_016: <NCA>"You should be their new chief."
MID_SE_Ism_Die_S_017: That's...maybe not a bad idea.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_S_018: They've got no god anymore. No chief to tell\n'em what to do. They're kind of lost.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_S_019: You know, exactly like I was when Orchel\nfound me.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_S_020: So, I guess you're going to disappear, now that\nyou've thrown some crumbs my way.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_S_021: But I hope you stick around.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_S_022: <RSDS>I'll be a chief this world's never seen—armed\nwith compassion. Kind of like Orchel.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_S_023: And one who leads with strength. Kind of like you.
MID_SE_Ism_Die_S_024: So, don't turn your back. You never know what\nus Har Hali warriors are going to get up to.